==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{uder|en|la|sine||without}} + {{m|la|diē}}, the ablative singular of {{m|la|diēs||a day}}. Literally meaning "without a day".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsʌɪni ˈdʌɪiː/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈsaɪni ˈdaɪi/}}
*  {{IPA|en|/ˈsɪneɪ ˈdiːeɪ/}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[without|Without]] [[specifying]] a [[date]] (for a [[future]] [[event]]); [[indefinitely]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1860|author={{w|Ellen Wood}}|title=East Lynne|page=6|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2005
|passage=Years ago […] he might have retrieved his position; but he had done what most people will do in such cases—put off the evil day '''''sine die''''', and gone on increasing his enormous list of debts.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1979|author={{w|André Brink}}|title=A Dry White Season|page=105|publisher=Vintage|year_published=1998
|passage=In anticipation of Dr Hassiem's release the inquest of Mr Ngubene's death, originally scheduled for 13 April, was postponed '''''sine die'''''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=1997|author={{w|Andrew Wong (politician)|Andrew Wong}}|title=Official Record of Proceedings—27 June 1997|journal=Official Record of Proceedings of the Hong Kong Legislative Council|url=https://www.legco.gov.hk/yr96-97/chinese/lc_sitg/floor/970627cd.doc|page=1407|text=In accordance with the Standing Orders of the Legislative Council, I now adjourn the Council, '''''sine die'''''.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|en|adjournment sine die}}

